# Section 6 settings.
#
# The notebooks, the course venv and the scripts all read the .env at the REPO ROOT,
# so append these lines there (from the repo root), then set AWS_PROFILE:
#   cat section-06-production-deployment/.env.example >> .env
# .env is git-ignored — never commit real values.

# ── AWS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Your AWS CLI profile. Log in first: aws sso login --profile <name>
AWS_PROFILE=your-profile-name
AWS_REGION=us-east-1
AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=us-east-1
# Used by the multi-agent lab's commands and setup_cognito.sh
REGION=us-east-1
# Empty = no AWS CLI pager, so deploy/cleanup scripts don't stop at "(END)"
AWS_PAGER=

# ── Model ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The labs default to global.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6, which needs the Anthropic
# use-case form (once per AWS account). Until it's approved, Amazon Nova works for
# every Section 6 lab — uncomment:
# BEDROCK_MODEL_ID=us.amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0

# ── Multi-agent lab: the Cognito test user created by setup_cognito.sh ──
# Pick your own password (8+ characters).
# COGNITO_USERNAME=testuser
# COGNITO_PASSWORD=ChangeMe-Passw0rd
